  "question": "Find the area in the first quadrant enclosed by the circle $x^2 + y^2 = 9$.",
  "answeroption": "D",
  "explanation": "Here $y=\\sqrt{9-x^2}$ for $0\\le x\\le 3$.<br /><br />Area $=\\int_{0}^{3}\\sqrt{9-x^2}dx$.<br /><br />Using the standard formula gives $\\frac{9\\pi}{4}$.<br /><br />Hence required area is $\\frac{9\\pi}{4}$ square units.",
